# Coverage audit (c4): otterPS's `otter run` compiles this program (every
# statement is in its compiled engine's subset), so it runs on
# src/native/OtterNativeRuntime.cs, not the interpreter: `length of` bytes
# is refused, .NET's own failures keep .NET's message in `otherwise into`,
# and a failure that is not an Otter error ends the program as the compiled
# engine's internal problem.
b is bytes from text "abc"
try
    say length of b
otherwise into reason
    say "length:" reason
.
d is date from "2024-01-15"
try
    add 100000 years to d
otherwise into reason
    say "years:" reason
.
try
    add 9000 years to d
otherwise into reason
    say "years past 9999:" reason
.
try
    add 200000 months to d
otherwise into reason
    say "months:" reason
.
try
    add 3000000 days to d
otherwise into reason
    say "days:" reason
.
try
    add 1000000000 days to d
otherwise into reason
    say "days out of range:" reason
.
try
    random number from 2147483647 to 2147483647 into top
    say top
otherwise into reason
    say "random:" reason
.
try
    set random seed to 30000000000
otherwise into reason
    say "seed:" reason
.
set random seed to 2.5
random number from 1 to 100 into pick
say "seeded:" pick
say "the last one is not caught:"
add 100000 years to d
say "never"
